# mutgap4_svc_invalidate_set_guest_valid: InvalidateResources (52) with only the set-guest-valid flag (the entry's fourth flag byte) on a private buffer whose host copy is newer: a fill listed with invalidateGuest left it guest-invalid and host-valid, so it needs a sync. The guest writes 0x33 over its page, 52 marks the guest copy valid, and SynchronizeResources (53) then has nothing to copy out: the 0x33 stays. In the service the private buffer is a detach buffer over the guest's pages, which the fill wrote at once and which ignores guest validity (tasks_objects_private).
